---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { contactEmail } from '../config';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy — omw"
  description="omw doesn't collect personal data. What the app and this website do and don't do."
  label="Privacy"
  heading="Your windows stay yours."
  sheet="Sheet 02 / Privacy"
>
  <section>
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>omw doesn't collect, store or sell personal data. There's no account, no analytics and no tracking, in the app or on this website.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      omw runs entirely on your Mac. Your layouts and settings are saved in <code>~/.config/omw/config.json</code> and never
      leave your computer.
    </p>
    <p>
      macOS asks you to grant omw Accessibility access. omw uses it only to find the windows on your screen and move them.
      Nothing it sees is recorded or sent anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      To check for updates, omw downloads a small update feed from GitHub, where releases are hosted. Like any web request,
      this shares your IP address and the omw version with GitHub. No other information about your Mac is sent. You can
      turn automatic checks off in Settings → General → Updates.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you install omw with Homebrew, Homebrew's own <a href="https://docs.brew.sh/Analytics">analytics policy</a> applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses no cookies, no analytics and no third-party scripts. Fonts are served from this site. The server may
      log standard request data such as IP address, time and browser, which is used only to run and secure the site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>, your email is used only to reply. You can ask
      what's stored about you or have it deleted at any time. The person responsible is listed on
      the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Last updated October 16, 2026.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
